 ## Operating characteristics
-* **Time Complexity:** The conversion time depends on the number of mesh faces and the grid resolution. On an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 with PyTorch 2.6.0+cu124 and CUDA 12.4, converting a mesh with 268k vertices and 280k faces at grid size 512 takes 27.1 ms warm time [S1, unofficial]. For a subdivided mesh with 3.6M vertices and 10.3M faces, it takes 82.1 ms warm time [S1, unofficial].
-* **Memory Complexity:** Memory usage scales with the number of active voxels and the attributes stored per voxel. For the 268k vertex mesh, warm peak memory is 939.7 MB [S1, unofficial]. For the 3.6M vertex mesh, it is 1836.8 MB [S1, unofficial].
